    "findings": [
      "Vm::call uses operands.split_off, yielding an argument-vector allocation and copy for nonzero argument counts in the inspected optimized native successful call path.",
      "Heap::find uses a hash-map ownership lookup and Any downcast. Two indirect type-id calls survive in native Vm::dispatch. WASI retains the equivalent calls inside Heap::find helpers.",
      "Vm::dispatch clones the primitive name before string dispatch.",
      "Inlining snail_rt_enter leaves threshold checks and conditional Vm::collect calls."
    ],
    "caveats": [
      "These structural findings identify retained work, not a measured division of runtime costs.",
      "This LTO experiment preserved the existing dynamic runtime; it did not compare fixed-layout Rust builtin accessors with equivalent directly emitted LLVM.",
      "Current source HEAD may contain documentation/experiment harness changes after the original benchmark commit 98f20132b44b8c0f4283d9149c0d6125da549722."
    ]
